  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 504.06 Distribution Valve Operation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 504.06 Distribution Valve Operation.\n\n(a) The owner of a PWS shall fully turn each distribution system valve either:\n\n(1) At least once every 12 months;\n\n(2) At the frequency identified in the PWS’s operations and maintenance manual or rules, provided that not less than 20% of the valves are operated annually and all valves are operated at least once every 5 years; or\n\n(3) Less frequently than every 5 years if a waiver is granted by the department pursuant to Env-Dw 202, because asset management and maintenance records, as applicable, demonstrate that a frequency of over 5 years satisfies valve operability objectives.\n\n(b) This activity shall be scheduled to minimize the potential impact on customers.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 504) #10465, eff 12-2-13; ss by #14006, eff 6-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw500.html"
